   "evidence": "TransitionCount.lean:240-249 \u2014 the body is `Equiv.ofFiberEquiv (fun c => Fintype.equivOfCardEq \u2026)` plus `Equiv.ofFiberEquiv_map`; `Equiv.ofFiberEquiv` is stated for arbitrary `{f : \u03b1 \u2192 \u03b3} {g : \u03b2 \u2192 \u03b3}` (mathlib/Mathlib/Logic/Equiv/Basic.lean:192), and `[Finite X]` is exactly the hypothesis needed since infinite fibers collapse to `Nat.card = 0`.",
   "file": "TauCeti/Combinatorics/Enumerative/TransitionCount.lean",
   "fix": "State it as `theorem occCount_exists_perm_comp {X : Type*} [Finite X] {u v : X \u2192 S} (h : \u2200 y, occCount u y = occCount v y) : \u2203 \u03c3 : Equiv.Perm X, v \u2218 \u03c3 = u` in TauCeti/Data/Fintype/Fiber.lean (proof unchanged after `classical; let _ := Fintype.ofFinite X`), and let `exists_perm_comp_of_transitionCount_eq` specialize it at `X := Fin (n + 1)`.",
   "issue": "`exists_perm_comp_of_occCount_eq {N : \u2115} {u v : Fin N \u2192 \u03b1}` is a purely index-agnostic statement about occCount fibers (its proof uses only `Equiv.ofFiberEquiv` and `Fintype.equivOfCardEq`; no `Fin.succ`/`castSucc`/`0`/`last`/arithmetic), so it is left at a special index type by the PR that generalizes `occCount` away from `Fin N`, and stays in `TauCeti` rather than beside the general API.",
   "line": "240"
  }
 ],
